message: "If you use this resource, please cite it using the metadata below. Add the DOI after the first archived public release."
title: "AI-Assisted Social Science Research: A Reason-Provenance Resource and Worked Case Study"
authors:
  - family-names: "Rudkin"
    given-names: "Simon"
    affiliation: "Department of Social Statistics, University of Manchester"
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  A social-science-facing resource and worked case study on the use of generative
  AI across a research workflow, with particular attention to reason provenance,
  attribution ambiguity, consequential research judgement, claim revision and
  evidential control.
keywords:
  - "social science"
  - "generative AI"
  - "research methods"
  - "reason provenance"
  - "research transparency"
  - "AI-assisted research"
  - "PISA"
